    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34212" root="فعم" body-key="f">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَعُمَ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَعُمَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَعَامَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُعُومَةٌ</span>, <i>It was,</i>
or <i>became, full;</i> said of the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاعِد</span> [or fore arm];
(S, K;) and of a vessel. (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَعُمَتْ</span>,
said of a woman, <i>She was,</i> or <i>became, full-formed,
and thick in her shank.</i> (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also 4, in
three places.

